                <pb facs="1047" n="951" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg951"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Dewey telegraphs entire island of Panay in possession of insurgents, except
                    Iloilo, which is defended by 800 Spanish troops. Foreign citizens beg for
                    American protection. Island of Negros has declared independence and desires
                    American protectorate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
